      <tag name="Reference.CriterionID" value="5" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="NC" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>b8dc3e97-98d0-4eab-a58d-b8681fc41c27</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#06</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD provide the ability to capture and update a dispensing status for each medication order.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="151" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="Reference.Alias" value="PHR_R2" />
      <tag name="Reference.FunctionID" value="PH.2.5.2" />
      <tag name="Reference.CriterionID" value="6" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="NC" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>64532419-1824-4e59-a395-7f0a2c83c448</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#07</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL present the list of medications to be self-administered.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="152" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="Reference.Alias" value="PHR_R2" />
      <tag name="Reference.FunctionID" value="PH.2.5.2" />
      <tag name="Reference.CriterionID" value="7" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="NC" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>a034568e-7434-4378-93b9-91f3aac75ce2</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#08</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide the ability to render the timing, route of administration, and dose of all medications on the medication list.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="153" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="Reference.Alias" value="PHR_R2" />
      <tag name="Reference.FunctionID" value="PH.2.5.2" />
      <tag name="Reference.CriterionID" value="8" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="C" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>0a6b15c5-4a33-46ea-b1ae-28c43cc003d6</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#09</name>
      <notes>The system MAY provide the ability to capture available instructions regarding the administration of selected items on the medication list (e.g., by receiving administration instruction from the family physician, or by downloading information from the pharmacy).</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="154" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="MAY" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="Reference.Alias" value="PHR_R2" />
      <tag name="Reference.FunctionID" value="PH.2.5.2" />
      <tag name="Reference.CriterionID" value="9" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="NC" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>6e8bad63-23b4-40da-9d95-44f4d294aa46</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#10</name>
      <notes>IF the system captures available instructions regarding the administration of selected items on the medication list, THEN the system MAY provide the ability for the PHR Account Holder to render available instructions regarding the administration of selected items on the medication list (e.g., to help the PHR Account Holder determine whether to discuss with their provider adjusting the dosing of Warfarin after receiving the results of an updated International Normalized Ratio (INR) laboratory test).</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="155" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="MAY" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="Reference.Alias" value="PHR_R2" />
      <tag name="Reference.FunctionID" value="PH.2.5.2" />
      <tag name="Reference.CriterionID" value="10" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="NC" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>af0cbac7-93a6-4a1b-9a2b-902015622c60</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#11</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD render a notification to the PHR Account Holder regarding a specific medication administration subject to the PHR Account Holder’s preconfigured modalities for transmitting various types of notifications. For example, on a specific date/time via text message, or for a specific event (such as strenuous exercise via email), or for a specific condition (such as failure to complete an activity of daily living via a phone call to a family member).</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="156" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="Reference.Alias" value="PHR_R2" />
      <tag name="Reference.FunctionID" value="PH.2.5.2" />
      <tag name="Reference.CriterionID" value="11" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="NC" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>c10fd2f1-ac05-4043-9d7e-0b235155d280</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#12</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD provide the ability to capture medication self-administration details (e.g., timestamps, observations, complications, and/or the reason that a medication dose was not taken). For example, a mother could capture an indication that her baby was unwilling or unable to swallow a pill/liquid.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="157" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="Reference.Alias" value="PHR_R2" />
      <tag name="Reference.FunctionID" value="PH.2.5.2" />
      <tag name="Reference.CriterionID" value="12" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="NC" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>46279ea6-15df-4064-8529-17e8b4a3f176</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#13</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD provide the ability for the PHR Account Holder to transmit refill (both refill and renewal) requests to a pharmacy or prescribing provider.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="158" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="Reference.Alias" value="PHR_R2" />
      <tag name="Reference.FunctionID" value="PH.2.5.2" />
      <tag name="Reference.CriterionID" value="13" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="C" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>e9ff608e-0449-4050-aa77-2eb766d7a34f</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#14</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD provide the ability to annotate the entire medication list with a field for text comments.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="159" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="Reference.Alias" value="PHR_R2" />
      <tag name="Reference.FunctionID" value="PH.2.5.2" />
      <tag name="Reference.CriterionID" value="14" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="C" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>2e75e83b-a722-4a28-8bf9-96532a9f3e4d</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#15</name>
      <notes>The system MAY provide the ability to render a medication list containing only medications selected by the PHR Account Holder.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="160" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="MAY" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="Reference.Alias" value="PHR_R2" />
      <tag name="Reference.FunctionID" value="PH.2.5.2" />
      <tag name="Reference.CriterionID" value="15" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="NC" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>f56cd433-3315-4500-a4f3-6173dcda604d</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#16</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide the ability for the PHR Account Holder to update the medication list by indicating those medications that are actually being taken.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="161" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="Reference.Alias" value="PHR_R2" />
      <tag name="Reference.FunctionID" value="PH.2.5.2" />
      <tag name="Reference.CriterionID" value="16" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="C" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>0815548e-a7ab-41e7-b246-e9711ce45455</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#17</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide the ability for the PHR Account Holder to maintain the medication list by updating the status of the medication self-administration (e.g., no longer being taken or completed the regime).</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="162" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="Reference.Alias" value="PHR_R2" />
      <tag name="Reference.FunctionID" value="PH.2.5.2" />
      <tag name="Reference.CriterionID" value="17" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="C" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>586fa9c6-8de2-4951-9306-65a54bf74317</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#18</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD provide the ability to capture, maintain, and render prescription and non-prescription items (including dietary supplements) as discrete data and/or as lists.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="163" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="Reference.Alias" value="PHR_R2" />
      <tag name="Reference.FunctionID" value="PH.2.5.2" />
      <tag name="Reference.CriterionID" value="18" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="NC" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>473fd3ed-86a2-4310-9aac-4a5d659799e5</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#19</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD provide the ability to receive current medications and a medication history from an external source (e.g., an EHR system, an insurance plan, a payer, or a pharmacy).</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="164" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="Reference.Alias" value="PHR_R2" />
      <tag name="Reference.FunctionID" value="PH.2.5.2" />
      <tag name="Reference.CriterionID" value="19" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="C" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>73713e83-b0a9-4e97-9284-10f5ebcdee7e</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#20</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD provide the ability to receive, maintain, and render information from an external source (e.g., from an EHR system or from a pharmacy system) regarding the difference between medications that were ordered and medications that were actually dispensed.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="165" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="Reference.Alias" value="PHR_R2" />
      <tag name="Reference.FunctionID" value="PH.2.5.2" />
      <tag name="Reference.CriterionID" value="20" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="NC" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>3910eaae-2209-4f2b-89cc-260912916e3a</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#21</name>
      <notes>The system MAY provide the ability to capture instructions regarding the cessation of selected items on the medication list. For example, the PHR Account holder could receive instructions from the family physician, the pharmacist, or from the medication manufacturer regarding behaviors that are permitted based on the cessation of a given medication. Another example is that the PHR Account Holder could be informed that the use of a blood thinner (e.g., Warfarin) must not be stopped abruptly. Finally, the PHR Account Holder could be informed that it is necessary to take the full course of a given prescribed medication.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="166" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="MAY" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="Reference.Alias" value="PHR_R2" />
      <tag name="Reference.FunctionID" value="PH.2.5.2" />
      <tag name="Reference.CriterionID" value="21" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="NC" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>f5a5d4e9-f35a-44ce-a115-c9ece28dec97</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#22</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD provide the ability to specify query selection criteria (e.g., encounter type (inpatient, ER...), how far to look back (query back to date), medications ordered and dispensed, over the counter medications).</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="90" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="CompilerInclusionReason" value="New from ProfileDefinition" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="N" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>c8dcd0ea-a095-423e-a6fa-e54a6fb0a216</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#23</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide the ability to capture, maintain and render the query/response for a the medication list associated with the most recent medication reconciliation event, for example:
&gt; Constrained to the last outpatient encounter, ER visit, discharge from inpatient or extended care encounter;
&gt; Constrained to EHR systems of other providers;
&gt; Constrained to event date/time, organization, practitioner, encounter type.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="91" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="CompilerInclusionReason" value="New from ProfileDefinition" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="N" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>c2b69b1e-11fa-4fe1-9b9e-a17d6a62159d</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#24</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD provide the ability to capture, maintain and render the most recent query/response for a medication list to the patient's pharmacy benefits manager (PBM) (e.g., a query via FHIR or API)</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="92" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="CompilerInclusionReason" value="New from ProfileDefinition" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="N" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>cfc54c50-c839-4296-9731-b8ac0f7fda37</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#25</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD provide the ability to capture, maintain and render the most recent query/response for a medication list to the patient's pharmacy dispensing system (e.g., a query via FHIR or API)</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="93" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="CompilerInclusionReason" value="New from ProfileDefinition" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="N" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>ab60bdfa-acb1-4990-84e3-9d868df51b38</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#26</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD provide the ability to capture, maintain and render the most recent query/response for a medication list to any system (e.g., EHR systems of other providers, PHR systems used by the patient).</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="94" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="CompilerInclusionReason" value="New from ProfileDefinition" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="N" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>28fd85f5-477f-4e06-9cda-8f3a3522889f</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#27</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL capture and maintain separate medication lists from each external system responding to a query, until a subsequent step which then disambiguates and incorporates each unique medication into a single list.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="100" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="CompilerInclusionReason" value="New from ProfileDefinition" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="N" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>bb53cd24-fbf8-4162-9404-d0c4ccc79e58</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#28</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide the ability to capture, maintain and render a list of source systems (and providers) from which current (active) or past medications were received.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="104" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="CompilerInclusionReason" value="New from ProfileDefinition" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="N" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>ad86a12f-31ca-4ef3-9d89-41a26e0022f5</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#29</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide the ability to capture, store and render the medication list from a previous patient-centric medication list management session.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="110" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="CompilerInclusionReason" value="New from ProfileDefinition" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="N" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>1060ae4d-0c73-4d93-b620-7b704436560f</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#30</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide the ability to capture, maintain and render the patient's current medication list, incorporating lists captured from external sources (i.e., an "as taken" medication list authored by the patient).</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="111" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="CompilerInclusionReason" value="New from ProfileDefinition" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="N" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>baceca3e-4567-48c4-85c9-f2a42a869c1e</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#31</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide the ability to determine the aggregation of medication lists from multiple sources via a disambiguation function.  Disambiguation compares the following elements to decide if medications match, partially match or do not match: generic name, trade (brand) name(s), dose, dose units, route, and frequency. </notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="112" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="CompilerInclusionReason" value="New from ProfileDefinition" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="N" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>1f0840d1-a079-4377-b589-9de4d2d54467</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#32</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide the ability to capture, maintain and render the results of disambiguation of the medication list. </notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="113" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="CompilerInclusionReason" value="New from ProfileDefinition" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="N" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>d6eed1c8-f9a3-4e6b-b47e-834f86ae08e7</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#33</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide the ability to render each medication using a reference source for representation of the medication name, dose, and other structured medication information (e.g., use of reference sources such as RxNorm, pharmacy compendia).</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="114" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="CompilerInclusionReason" value="New from ProfileDefinition" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="N" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>5529e340-9356-4305-8144-962b5898a9aa</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#34</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide the ability to capture, maintain and render confirmation that the patient is currently taking a particular medication, including medication name, dose, dose units, route, frequency, comments, and adherence details.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="118" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="CompilerInclusionReason" value="New from ProfileDefinition" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="N" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>8718894d-136e-49fa-a0f4-56bfe1f1df99</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#35</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide the ability to capture, maintain and render the addition of a medication to the patient medication list, including medication generic and brand name(s), dose, dose units, route, frequency, comments, adherence details, and ordering prescriber, using a reference source for representation and management of structured medication information (e.g., type-ahead pick lists, duplicate checking, presriber information). </notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="122" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="CompilerInclusionReason" value="New from ProfileDefinition" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="N" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>cebbbdc3-d911-49c1-8f94-c358cdd95923</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#36</name>
      <notes>If a medication has been added, the system SHALL determine whether new drug-drug interactions are identified.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="124" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="CompilerInclusionReason" value="New from ProfileDefinition" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="N" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>4a1fcb38-bee7-4bb6-8980-a0e4a3b38d1a</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#37</name>
      <notes>IF drug-drug interactions or other clinical safety related risks are identified, THEN the system SHALL provide the ability to manage related information (e.g., source of concern, severity of potential interaction, alerting user that interaction may need to be reviewed by clinician).</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="125" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="Y" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="CompilerInclusionReason" value="New from ProfileDefinition" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="N" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>7504ef9b-8f26-4b2c-a43c-71c977eabff3</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#38</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide the ability to capture, maintain and render the modification (change) of a medication on the patient medication list, including dose, frequency, comments, and adherence, reason for update, and ordering prescriber. 

</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="127" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="CompilerInclusionReason" value="New from ProfileDefinition" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="N" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>1ab3222a-afe8-45d9-8055-6512b5cb0219</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#39</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide the ability to update (i.e., modify/change) a medication after it has been added to the medication list.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="128" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="CompilerInclusionReason" value="New from ProfileDefinition" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="N" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>0f47e705-bd4e-47ed-9503-cdca9ddb8ee9</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#40</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide the ability to capture, maintain and render a notation that the patient is not currently taking a medication and the current status of the medication. Status includes that the medication is:
&gt; Stopped, as directed by clinician;
&gt; Stopped by patient;
&gt; On hold, as directed by clinician;
&gt; On hold by patient.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="131" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="CompilerInclusionReason" value="New from ProfileDefinition" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="N" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>60ac99e1-1624-4ff0-88f4-737f0fa05139</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#41</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide the ability to capture, maintain and render the reason the patient is not taking a medication (e.g., taking alternative medication; side effects / adverse reaction / intolerance; course completed; no longer indicated; cannot afford; not covered by insurance; etc.).</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="132" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="CompilerInclusionReason" value="New from ProfileDefinition" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="N" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>79dd7b09-05d5-4d7f-a735-f39ff27ef4a2</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#42</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD provide the ability to capture the number of doses remaining for each medication.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="134" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="CompilerInclusionReason" value="New from ProfileDefinition" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="N" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>9da7a0c3-81b1-4950-8e35-83d0112d7346</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#43</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD provide the ability to capture, maintain and render medication refill requests based on remaining dose thresholds (e.g., system calculation to message patient to request a refill of a regularly taken medication).</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="137" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="CompilerInclusionReason" value="New from ProfileDefinition" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="N" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>3ff92a46-6d38-41c6-98de-12b508929cea</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#44</name>
      <notes>The system MAY provide the ability to determine upcoming refills needed from calculations based on pill counts, dates and frequencies as ordered.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="138" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="MAY" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="CompilerInclusionReason" value="New from ProfileDefinition" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="N" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>217d23d1-a57e-403b-86f3-52d0db9a311c</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#45</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL present visual feedback to the patient (e.g., row color changes, strikethrough, other indicators) as the status of each medication is actioned upon during reconciliation. </notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="139" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="CompilerInclusionReason" value="New from ProfileDefinition" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="N" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>f20ff071-d771-4de5-ac7f-0ee61cdb3a30</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#46</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL present visual feedback to the patient (e.g., absence of change in row color) highlighting medications awaiting review during reconciliation.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="140" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="CompilerInclusionReason" value="New from ProfileDefinition" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="N" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>1af0424e-3d0d-4b32-8069-dc42df5fcb7e</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#47</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide the ability to render reports for printing or export (e.g., using a style sheet) per the preference of the patient - recommended presentation examples include: 
&gt; Grouped by time of day, then alpha sort of generic (+ trade) name of medications with dosages as grouped sections (e.g., list of medications taken once a day in the AM);
&gt; Calendar (grid) week view, with x-axis as day of week and y-axis as time of day;
&gt; Include graphical version options with color pictures of the pills, pill markings;
&gt; Medical Assistant view – alpha sort of generic + (trade) name, dosage, and timing; with patient notes;
&gt; Clinician view – by discipline, grouped by confirm / not taking / update / add, then alpha sort of generic + (trade) name, dosage, and timing; with patient notes;
&gt; Patient-generated medication list (as electronic output) – all fields.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="145" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="CompilerInclusionReason" value="New from ProfileDefinition" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="N" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>8484fcbd-dd75-4b16-b562-f3022de2f5de</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.2#48</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide the ability to transmit a reviewed and/or updated medication list following patient-performed medication reconciliation (e.g., in preparation for an upcoming encounter):
&gt; Assembled as a data bundle (e.g., as a FHIR data bundle per a FHIR specification)
&gt; Incuding patient annotations.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>4309c0e6-5488-41be-be93-74aa5b8a0aca</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="149" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="CompilerInclusionReason" value="New from ProfileDefinition" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="N" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>222ed2a6-7618-4381-9fe0-44501b10d8e4</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.4</name>
      <alias>PH.2.5.4</alias>
      <notes>$ST$Manage the PHR Account Holder’s list of known allergens and adverse reactions with all pertinent information.$DE$Allergies, intolerances, sensitivities, and adverse reactions must be reviewed with every new prescription to avoid an allergic reaction. 

Environmental and food allergens should be listed and maintained here, as well as allergies to bee sting, sunlight, or substances (e.g., latex, metal, or contrast media (such as dye).

Example(s): The system SHALL provide the ability to enter, store, update and display information related to allergic and adverse reactions or intolerances to drug and non-drug allergens or substances.$EX$</notes>
      <stereotype>Function</stereotype>
      <type>Feature</type>
      <parentId>c6eaa647-30b2-4b00-8574-00e5c223b7e1</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="179" />
      <tag name="Reference.Alias" value="PHR_R2" />
      <tag name="Reference.FunctionID" value="PH.2.5.4" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="C" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>afe67356-2550-4087-80ed-d404dc9200c3</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.4#01</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide the ability to manage information related to allergy, intolerance, and adverse reaction to drugs, foods, or environmental triggers as unique, discrete entries (including, for example, substances such as latex, metal, and contrast media (such as dye)).</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>222ed2a6-7618-4381-9fe0-44501b10d8e4</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="180" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="Reference.Alias" value="PHR_R2" />
      <tag name="Reference.FunctionID" value="PH.2.5.4" />
      <tag name="Reference.CriterionID" value="1" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="NC" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>1a09aee1-6bd1-45f1-9e7d-34dce31b1f4a</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.4#02</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD provide the ability to capture the reason for entry of the allergy, intolerance or adverse reaction.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>222ed2a6-7618-4381-9fe0-44501b10d8e4</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="181" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="Reference.Alias" value="PHR_R2" />
      <tag name="Reference.FunctionID" value="PH.2.5.4" />
      <tag name="Reference.CriterionID" value="2" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="NC" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>5cc7829c-23b8-4f97-98ab-c22feeebc267</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.4#03</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide the ability to manage information related to allergic and adverse reactions to drug and non-drug allergens or substances.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>222ed2a6-7618-4381-9fe0-44501b10d8e4</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="182" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="Reference.Alias" value="PHR_R2" />
      <tag name="Reference.FunctionID" value="PH.2.5.4" />
      <tag name="Reference.CriterionID" value="3" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="NC" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>b4854bf7-8cdb-46e7-bf70-de88983a311a</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.4#04</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide the ability to manage information regarding the reaction type.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>222ed2a6-7618-4381-9fe0-44501b10d8e4</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="183" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="Reference.Alias" value="PHR_R2" />
      <tag name="Reference.FunctionID" value="PH.2.5.4" />
      <tag name="Reference.CriterionID" value="4" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="NC" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>967e5246-92af-4c4e-b581-b9f661102f9f</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.4#05</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide the ability to manage information regarding the severity of a reaction.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>222ed2a6-7618-4381-9fe0-44501b10d8e4</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="184" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="Reference.Alias" value="PHR_R2" />
      <tag name="Reference.FunctionID" value="PH.2.5.4" />
      <tag name="Reference.CriterionID" value="5" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="NC" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>922bb4a5-3bd6-4db8-a524-cc2548f6648a</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.4#06</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD provide the ability to maintain associated allergic reactions to the prevention protocols and/or medications being taken.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>222ed2a6-7618-4381-9fe0-44501b10d8e4</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="185" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="Reference.Alias" value="PHR_R2" />
      <tag name="Reference.FunctionID" value="PH.2.5.4" />
      <tag name="Reference.CriterionID" value="6" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="NC" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>728320e4-8235-4f3f-b5bb-0988d3828608</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.4#07</name>
      <notes>The system SHALL provide the ability to manage an indication regarding the negation of a health reaction (e.g., No Known Allergies (NKA), No Known Drug Allergies (NKDA), No Known Food Allergies (NKFA), No Known Sensitivies, or No Known Intolerances).</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>222ed2a6-7618-4381-9fe0-44501b10d8e4</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="186" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHALL" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="Reference.Alias" value="PHR_R2" />
      <tag name="Reference.FunctionID" value="PH.2.5.4" />
      <tag name="Reference.CriterionID" value="7" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="NC" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>9bab0b23-1e5f-42da-be8d-fddd34989748</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.4#08</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD provide the ability to capture the source of allergy, intolerance, and adverse reaction information.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>222ed2a6-7618-4381-9fe0-44501b10d8e4</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="187" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="Reference.Alias" value="PHR_R2" />
      <tag name="Reference.FunctionID" value="PH.2.5.4" />
      <tag name="Reference.CriterionID" value="8" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="NC" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>ef7881da-b428-44f4-b51d-00d0adc14799</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.4#09</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD provide the ability to capture and maintain an indication regarding the deactivation of an item on the allergy, intolerance, and/or adverse reaction lists.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>222ed2a6-7618-4381-9fe0-44501b10d8e4</parentId>
      <tag name="Row" value="188" />
      <tag name="Optionality" value="SHOULD" />
      <tag name="Conditional" value="N" />
      <tag name="Dependent" value="N" />
      <tag name="Reference.Alias" value="PHR_R2" />
      <tag name="Reference.FunctionID" value="PH.2.5.4" />
      <tag name="Reference.CriterionID" value="9" />
      <tag name="Reference.ChangeIndicator" value="NC" />
      <tag name="Priority" value="EN" />
    </object>
    <object>
      <id>7f4129f3-e929-4600-94c3-cccb2231f973</id>
      <name>PH.2.5.4#10</name>
      <notes>The system SHOULD provide the ability to capture the reason for the deactivation of an item on the allergy, intolerance, and/or adverse reaction lists.</notes>
      <stereotype>Criteria</stereotype>
      <type>Requirement</type>
      <parentId>222ed2a6-7618-4381-9fe0-44501b10d8e4</parentId>
